From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nate Isern <nate@oxy.so>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Paint the native browser UI from the profile's Bloom preset

Changing the theme in astro://settings has to re-colour the toolbar, the tab
strip, the omnibox and the menus, not only the page that offered the control.
This is the one call that lets it.

WHY HERE, AND WHY LAST

`AddChromeColorMixers` is where every Chromium mixer is installed, and a
ColorProvider resolves a ColorId through the LAST mixer that has a recipe for
it. Appending after `key.app_controller` therefore overrides upstream's
palette without editing any of it -- the alternative considered and rejected
was patching `theme_properties.cc`, which would have meant editing colour
values in place, in a file that churns every Chromium roll.

`AddAstroColorMixers` is not unconditional. It returns immediately under
forced colours, under the increased-contrast system setting, and when the
profile has a theme extension installed, because in each of those the user
has already answered the question this mixer would answer. The mapping from
Bloom token to ColorId is hand-written and reviewed in
chrome/browser/oxy/ui/astro_color_mixer.cc; the colour VALUES are generated
from Bloom's own tokens.json and nothing computes a colour anywhere in the
path.

THE BUILD EDGE IS PART OF THIS PATCH, NOT A FOLLOW-UP

`//chrome/browser/ui/color:mixers` gains a dependency on
`//chrome/browser/oxy:theming` in the same diff, because a hook whose target
is not in the build graph is exactly the defect this repository already has
one of: the whole overlay compiled to zero objects for want of a single edge
(#7, and its repair, 057-oxy-webui-build-edge.patch). A call and the edge that
makes it link are one change.

`:theming` is a separate target from the overlay's WebUI controllers precisely
so this edge can exist: it depends on //chrome/browser/themes and
//chrome/browser/ui/color:color_headers and NOT on //chrome/browser/ui, so
adding it here introduces no cycle.

Owned by https://github.com/OxyHQ/Astro/issues/24.
---
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/color/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/ui/color/BUILD.gn
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/color/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/color/BUILD.gn
@@ -52,6 +52,7 @@ source_set("mixers") {
     ":color_headers",
     "//build:branding_buildflags",
     "//chrome/app/theme:theme_resources",
+    "//chrome/browser/oxy:theming",
     "//chrome/browser/task_manager/common",
     "//chrome/browser/ui:ui_features",
     "//chrome/common/themes:autogenerated_theme_util",
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/color/chrome_color_mixers.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/color/chrome_color_mixers.cc
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/color/chrome_color_mixers.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/color/chrome_color_mixers.cc
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include "base/containers/fixed_flat_map.h"
 #include "base/functional/bind.h"
 #include "base/no_destructor.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/oxy/ui/astro_color_mixer.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/color/chrome_color_id.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/color/chrome_color_mixer.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/color/material_chrome_color_mixer.h"
@@ -81,4 +82,10 @@ void AddChromeColorMixers(ui::ColorProvider* provider,
   if (key.app_controller) {
     key.app_controller->AddColorMixers(provider, key);
   }
+
+  // Astro's Bloom colour preset, last, because the last mixer added is the one
+  // whose recipes win. It stands down entirely under forced colours, the
+  // increased-contrast system setting, and an installed theme extension --
+  // see chrome/browser/oxy/ui/astro_color_mixer.cc.
+  astro::AddAstroColorMixers(provider, key);
 }
